# Horizontal tabs: HT, HTS, TBC, CHT, CBT and DECST8C.

test tab stops start at every eighth column
spec VT510 DECST8C and xterm ctlseqs: tab stops at column 9, 17, ...
size 20 2
feed a\tb\tc
screen
|a       b       c   |

test a tab does not erase what it passes
spec ECMA-48 8.3.60 HT: the active position moves, nothing is written
size 20 2
feed ab\tc
screen
|ab      c           |

test a tab from the last stop goes to the last column
spec VT510 HT: with no more tab stops the cursor moves to the right margin
size 20 2
feed \e[1;17H\tx
screen
|                   x|
cursor 1,20

test a tab does not wrap
spec VT510 HT: HT does not cause text to auto wrap
size 20 2
feed \e[1;20H\tx
screen
|                   x|

test a tab from a stop goes to the next one
spec VT510 HT: moves the cursor to the next tab stop
size 20 2
feed \e[1;9H\tx
screen
|                x   |

test HTS sets a tab stop at the cursor
spec VT510 HTS: a tab stop at the column of the cursor; xterm ctlseqs ESC H
size 20 2
feed \e[1;4H\eH\r\tx
screen
|   x                |

test HTS leaves the other stops
spec VT510 HTS: does not affect the other horizontal tab stops
size 20 2
feed \e[1;4H\eH\r\t\tx
screen
|        x           |

test TBC 0 clears the stop at the cursor
spec VT510 TBC: Ps = 0 clears the tab stop at the cursor
size 20 2
feed \e[1;9H\e[0g\r\tx
screen
|                x   |

test TBC without a parameter is TBC 0
spec VT510 TBC: 0 or none (default)
size 20 2
feed \e[1;9H\e[g\r\tx
screen
|                x   |

test TBC 3 clears all stops
spec VT510 TBC: Ps = 3 clears all tab stops
size 20 2
feed \e[3g\r\tx
screen
|                   x|

test other TBC parameters are ignored
spec xterm ctlseqs TBC: the VT100 ignores codes other than 0 and 3
size 20 2
feed \e[1;9H\e[2g\r\tx
screen
|        x           |

test DECST8C restores the stops every eight columns
spec VT510 DECST8C and xterm ctlseqs CSI ? 5 W
known-fail: alacritty – CSI ? 5 W does not bring back the default stops after CSI 3 g
size 20 2
feed \e[3g\e[?5W\r\tx
screen
|        x           |

test CHT moves forward over tab stops
spec VT510 CHT; xterm ctlseqs CSI Ps I
size 20 2
feed \e[2I
cursor 1,17

test CHT defaults to one stop
spec VT510 CHT default 1
size 20 2
feed \e[I
cursor 1,9

test CHT stops at the last column
convention there is no tab stop past the right margin, so the cursor stops there
size 20 2
feed \e[9I
cursor 1,20

test CBT moves back to the previous stop
spec VT510 CBT; xterm ctlseqs CSI Ps Z
size 20 2
feed \e[1;12H\e[Z
cursor 1,9

test CBT by several stops stays on the first column
spec VT510 CBT: the active position stays at column one
size 20 2
feed \e[1;12H\e[2Z
cursor 1,1

test CBT from a stop goes to the one before
spec VT510 CBT: the n-th preceding tab stop
size 20 2
feed \e[1;17H\e[Z
cursor 1,9

test CBT on the first column stays
spec VT510 CBT: the active position stays at column one
size 20 2
feed \e[Z
cursor 1,1

test a stop set by HTS is used by CBT
spec VT510 CBT and HTS
size 20 2
feed \e[1;5H\eH\e[1;7H\e[Z
cursor 1,5

test tab stops cover the columns a resize adds
convention new columns get the default stops (every eighth column)
size 20 2
resize 30 2
feed \e[1;17H\tx
screen
|                        x     |

test a reset restores the default tab stops
spec VT510 RIS: restores the default settings
size 20 2
feed \e[3g\ec\tx
screen
|        x           |

test CBT with every stop cleared stops at the first column
spec VT510 CBT: if the active position would pass the left margin it stops at the left margin
known-fail: alacritty – CBT stays where it is when there is no stop to go back to
size 20 2
feed \e[3g\e[1;5H\e[Z
cursor 1,1
